@startuml
title Merge Request Validation Lane
left to right direction
skinparam Shadowing false
skinparam DefaultFontName DejaVu Sans
skinparam BackgroundColor white
skinparam ArrowColor #1d4f73
skinparam Rectangle {
  BorderColor #1d4f73
  BackgroundColor #eef6fb
  FontColor #0f172a
  RoundCorner 12
}
skinparam Note {
  BorderColor #8b6f2f
  BackgroundColor #fff7d6
  FontColor #3f3420
}

rectangle "Feature branch push" as push
rectangle "Plain branch push does not run CI" as no_push #fff4e5
rectangle "Open or update merge request" as mr
rectangle "Verify\nmerge-request-description-check\nformat-and-vet" as verify
rectangle "Test\nunit-tests\nkubectl-splunk-tests\noss-scan (advisory)" as test
rectangle "Build\nbuild-stage-image" as build
rectangle "Image scan\nscan-stage-image-trivy" as scan
rectangle "Smoke fanout on disposable EKS\nall smoke suites in parallel" as smoke #eefbf1

push --> no_push
push --> mr
mr --> verify
verify --> test
test --> build
build --> scan
scan --> smoke

note bottom of no_push
GitLab uses the MR as the normal branch-validation trigger
and suppresses duplicate push pipelines once the MR exists.
end note
@enduml
